<title>FINLAND: Foreign holdings of Finnish small-caps down in Nov.</title>
<headline>Foreign holdings of Finnish small-caps down in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign holdings in some Finnish small-cap stocks fell in November, but overall foreign ownership of Finnish companies registered in the Central Share Register (OKR) edged up to 27.2 percent of shares in issue from 27.0 percent at end-October, OKR said in its monthly review.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in mobile phones maker Benefon fell nearly 4.5 percentage points in November to 43.66 percent -- down more than 10 percentage points compared to end-1995.</p>
<p>Another high-tech small-cap firm, Efore, saw foreign ownership fall to 24.74 percent by end-November from 31.78 percent a month earlier. It was 45.56 percent at end-1995.</p>
<p>Following the EU Commission's rejection of wholesaler Kesko's acquisition of domestic competitor Tuko, foreign ownership in Kesko fell to 16.13 percent from 17.70.</p>
<p>At the turn of the year, foreign shareholders owned 13.80 percent of Kesko.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in telecoms blue-chip Nokia was unchanged at slightly below 71 percent.</p>
